HOW TO BUILD - S8 Docker Kernel
================================

Tested on: Ubuntu 22.04/24.04 64-bit (GCP e2-medium, 4 vCPU)

PREREQUISITES
-------------

1. Install build tools:

   sudo apt-get update
   sudo apt-get install -y git make bc bison flex libssl-dev \
       libncurses5-dev gcc-aarch64-linux-gnu zip python3

2. Clone this repo:

   git clone <repo-url>
   cd <repo-dir>

BUILD SCRIPTS
-------------

Scripts are provided. Check the SETUP section at the top
of each script and adjust paths to your machine if needed.

  clean.sh  - wipes the source tree (make mrproper) and deletes
              the output directory. Run this for a fresh build.

  edit.sh   - opens menuconfig to enable/disable kernel options,
              saves your changes back to the defconfig.

  build.sh  - full build: compiles the kernel, repacks boot.img,
              creates a TWRP-flashable zip.
              Output: s8-docker-kernel.zip

  pack.py   - (used by build.sh) repacks boot.img with the new
              kernel. Updates the header to fit any kernel size.

STEPS TO BUILD
--------------

1. # cleanup (optional, for fresh build)
   ./clean.sh

2. # edit kernel config (optional)
   ./edit.sh

3. # build (this takes a while, go grab a coffee)
   ./build.sh

   If it finishes without errors, you'll get s8-docker-kernel.zip
   in the repo folder. Flash it in TWRP.

NOTE
----

- Always build with a clean ramdisk (no Magisk). Flash Magisk
  separately after installing the kernel.
- base/base-boot.img is the XDA kernel's boot.img, used as the ramdisk
  source for repacking.
